    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. The repository has a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`), whose two tests both pass, along with a clean full build.\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged owner deletion from a hard delete to a soft delete:\n\n**Domain / persistence**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean column (`nullable = false`, defaults to `false`) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()`.\n- `db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added a `deleted BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE` column to the `owners` table. (Tests run on HSQLDB with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change is required there; the others are updated for parity.)\n\n**API surface**\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct maps it automatically. A created/fetched owner now reports `deleted`.\n\n**Behavior**\n- `service/ClinicServiceImpl.deleteOwner` \u2014 now sets `deleted = true` and saves (retaining the row) instead of `ownerRepository.delete(owner)`. `DELETE /api/owners/{id}` still returns `204` (2xx), and `GET` afterwards returns the owner with `deleted: true`.\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1` \u2014 the create endpoint's duplicate/identity checks now skip deleted owners: `rejectDuplicateIdentity` (identity/telephone), `rejectHouseholdDuplicate` (household), and `findPossibleDuplicate` (soft-match) each filter out `existing.isDeleted()`. A normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.\n\nA newly created owner has `deleted` false (entity default), confirmed by `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains`; the ignore-deleted behavior is confirmed by `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck`.",
